# The first three rows of the kernel's whole process table, as sysctl with CTL_KERN, KERN_PROC,
# KERN_PROC_ALL returned them on devthrottle-mac-mini (Apple M4, macOS 26.5.2, arm64) on
# 2026-10-15. One row is 648 bytes, so this is 1944 bytes. The machine had 657 processes at the
# time; only three are kept, because the point is the layout of a row, not the size of a machine.
#
# What the operating system itself said these three rows hold, printed from a C program using
# its own headers at the moment of capture:
#   row 0: pid 37254, parent 37240, user 501, name "dumptable",       started 1792091094.675943
#   row 1: pid 37240, parent 62661, user 501, name "zsh",             started 1792091094.284246
#   row 2: pid 37232, parent 1,     user 501, name "mdworker_shared", started 1792091093.467666
